{"name":"Megaman Helmet","hex":"#0058f8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"megaman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very large or powerful man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/megaman"},{"term":"helmet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, protective head covering, typically part of armour.","That which resembles a helmet in form, position, etc.\nThe upper part of a chemist's retort."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with, or as if with, a helmet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helmet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mega Man","blocks":[{"text":"Mega Man is a video game franchise developed and published by Capcom, featuring the eponymous protagonist. The original game was released for the Nintendo Entertainment System in 1987, and spawned a franchise that expanded to over 50 games on multiple systems. As of July 2026, the series had sold a total of 45 million units worldwide.\nMega Man has been popular among gamers and has been reimagined and evolved as a video game character for over 30 years."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man","wikidata":"Q7565689"},{"title":"Helmet","blocks":[{"text":"A helmet is a form of protective gear worn to protect the head. More specifically, a helmet complements the skull in protecting the human brain. Ceremonial or symbolic helmets without protective function are sometimes worn. Soldiers wear combat helmets, often made from Kevlar or other lightweight synthetic fibers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_Wide_Variety_Of_Helmets.png/330px-A_Wide_Variety_Of_Helmets.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helmet","wikidata":"Q173603"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f1/Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png/250px-Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte